y, uncooperative. Communication: issues. Responsibility: not mentioned.\n\nCandidate C: reliability: known 100% reliable. Crew cooperation: creates positive atmosphere. Decision quality: can make correct decisions quickly. Technical competence: not directly mentioned but maybe implied. Stress resilience: not mentioned. Communication: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric. Education: not willing. So strong on reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication issues.\n\nCandidate D: reliability: not mentioned. Stress resilience: responds adequately to unexpected events. Technical competence: solves problems extremely well, concentration. Decision quality? solves problems well. Responsibility: takes responsibility seriously. Crew cooperation: arrogant, weak leadership. Communication: maybe issues. Adaptability: good.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best overall. Candidate C seems strong on reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication issues and lack of further education. Candidate B strong on reliability, stress, technical, but interpersonal issues. Candidate D strong on problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but arrogance and weak leadership. Candidate A strong on anticipation, leadership, but unorganized, not good at criticism.\n\nWhich is best? The role requires crew cooperation and communication. Candidate C creates positive atmosphere, but difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric may affect. However \"creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\" suggests good crew cooperation despite communication difficulty? Could be contradictory. But difficulty communicating ideas may affect clarity in cockpit. Egocentric also concerning.\n\nCandidate B's grumpy/uncooperative is serious for crew cooperation. Candidate D's arrogance also serious. Candidate A's unorganized and not good at criticism may affect reliability.\n\nThus maybe Candidate C is the strongest overall: reliability, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere, quick decisions, 100% reliable. Communication issues are a concern but maybe less severe than grumpiness/uncooperative? However difficulty communicating ideas could be safety-critical. But we can ask other panel members for more info on C's communication. But we have to decide now.\n\nWe can argue that Candidate C's strengths outweigh concerns, and that his reliability and decision quality are critical. We can propose provisional recommendation for Candidate C, while acknowledging concerns.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's points and bring new evidence. So we can say: I appreciate Agent 2's focus on B, but I think C's reliability and decision speed are more crucial, and his positive crew atmosphere mitigates communication concerns. Provide evidence: known 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, can make correct decisions quickly. Also note concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Argue that these are less severe than B's grumpy/uncooperative.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\".\n\nLet's craft message: \"I agree reliability and stress are important, but I think Candidate C's proven reliability and decision quality, plus positive crew atmosphere, make him a stronger overall fit. While he has communication challenges, his ability to make correct decisions quickly and his 100% reliability are critical for safety. Compared to B's interpersonal issues, C's crew atmosphere suggests better cooperation. Therefore I propose Candidate C.\"\n\nMake sure to reference Agent 2's points.\n\nProceed."}
